From 3322eda29a71f142654f1835e2e1436dbd5c2c37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:03:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(assets): asset modes -- HF image-to-3D vs LLM +
 OpenSCAD per request, both variants kept per part, HF cached and warmed

- asset_mode "hf" | "llm_scad" | "auto" from the session context (/agent/command, /voice/command),
  the /parts/search body and ?mode= on part.json / model.glb; POST /parts/{id}/model?mode= -> pending/ready
- variants model.hf.glb / model.scad.glb / model.auto.glb (+ asset.<v>.json) side by side; model.glb and
  part.json follow the mode asked for last; legacy parts adopted (an ai_mesh model is the hf variant)
- asset.mode + asset.note (why the preferred tier didn't make it); asset.made_by names the Hunyuan Space
  (hf:tencent/Hunyuan3D-2.1) or the OpenSCAD writer (xai:grok-4.7 + openscad)
- HF: raw Hunyuan mesh cached by photo hash (one Space call per photo, ever); an ai_mesh variant is never
  rebuilt; server/hf_warm.py warms searched parts ahead of need, one at a time, backing off on the ZeroGPU
  quota; GET /assets/hf-warm; python -m server.warm --hf for every cached part
- llm_scad: Grok's OpenSCAD in the background (minutes) with the template meanwhile; no openscad binary on
  the server = the template, labelled
- tests: tests/test_asset_mode.py (29, HF/LLM/OpenSCAD stubbed); suite 1469 passed (3 pre-existing
  pipeline failures: os.sched_getaffinity on macOS)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
